SIZE(1)                     User Commands                  SIZE(1)

NAME
    size - print the sizes of the sections of object files

SYNOPSIS
    size [-ABGdotxf] [--format=format] [--radix=radix] [--common] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    size prints the sizes of the sections of ELF64 objects, shared objects,
    programs and archives of them. The default file is a.out. The output
    matches GNU size.

FORMATS
    -B, --format=berkeley   text, data and bss columns (default)
    -A, --format=sysv       one line per section with size and address
    -G, --format=gnu        text, data, bss and total columns

OPTIONS
    -d, -o, -x              print numbers in decimal, octal or hexadecimal
    --radix=8|10|16         select the radix by its value
    -t, --totals            print a line with the totals (Berkeley and GNU)
    --common                add the size of common symbols to bss
    -f                      ignored

SEE ALSO
    nm(1), strings(1), readelf(1)
